'''Wrath''' is a [[mini-boss]] based on one of the [[wikipedia:Seven Deadly Sins|Seven Deadly Sins]].

== Behavior ==
* Wrath wanders around the room randomly, occasionally standing still.
* Throws a {{E|Bomb}} towards Isaac if he is in line of sight and then attempts to run away from the bomb.
** Wrath takes only 20 damage (as opposed to the usual {{dlc|nr}} 60 / {{dlc|r}} 100) from his own bombs.
Wrath deals a full heart of damage (both bombs and contact).

== Notes ==
* {{dlc|anr}} Occasionally, 2 regular Wraths appear in a Mini-Boss Room and the boss message will display "Isaac vs {{E|Super Wrath}}".
* Isaac's bombs and {{i|Epic Fetus}} missiles deal 200 damage to Wrath regardless of modifiers or damage stat.
* {{dlc|nr}} Wrath can drop {{i|Mr. Boom}} even if Isaac has already encountered/possessed it. 

== Unlockable [[Achievement]]s ==
{{achievement text | The Book of Sin }}

== Trivia ==
* Wrath's behavior, his room layouts (most of the time), and his appearance are references to the ''[[Wikipedia:Bomberman|Bomberman]]'' series of games.
* The item {{i|Mr. Mega}} gives Isaac's head a similar appearance to Wrath's.
* The [[wikipedia:Seven Deadly Sins|Seven Deadly Sins]] that these mini-bosses are based upon are, in Christian teachings, a classification of vices from which all others are derived from.
* Wrath's absence of eyes could be a reference to the expression "blind rage".

